# Micro OS — the magic of a program of this system (the MOX1 format).
#
# This is our record and not one of Magdir: a file of /bin is a MOX1 image
# (ADR 0016), and the header of the format is four bytes no upstream database
# knows. It is the first rule of the database, so that a program of the system
# is named by the system and not mistaken for data.
#
# The fields are the header of components/kernel/include/kernel/exec.h:
# magic at 0, version at 4, the flags at 8, and the machine at 28.
0	string		MOX1		Micro OS MOX1 executable
!:mime	application/x-microos-mox
!:ext	mox
>4	lelong		1		\b, version 1
>4	lelong		2		\b, version 2
>8	lelong		0		\b, no flags
>28	lelong		0		\b, x86-64
>28	lelong		1		\b, Xtensa
